<title>UK: World rubber stocks rise in July.</title>
<headline>World rubber stocks rise in July.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>World stocks of both natural and synthetic rubber rose in July 1996, by 10,000 and 40,000 tonnes respectively, according to latest figures from the International Rubber Study Group.</p>
<p>    Data in thousand tonnes  --  JULY'96    JUN'96    JUL'95</p>
<p> Natural production			510	 460	 520</p>
<p> Natural consumption		     500	 500	 490</p>
<p> Natural stocks			  1,530     1,520     1,550</p>
<p> Synthetic production		    810	 790	 790</p>
<p> Synthetic consumption		   770	 780	 730</p>
<p> Synthetic stocks			2,090     2,050     2,040</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
